  "⛔_the_browser_rung_was_tried_and_refused": {
    "_what": "The three free-to-read series were re-requested through a real headless Chromium, visiting the article landing page first so the request carried whatever cookie it sets.",
    "result": "All three answered HTTP 403 again — and the browser genuinely ran: it returned real HTML error bodies of 5.8 KB, 5.8 KB and 832 KB rather than the 2 KB stub plain urllib gets. Elsevier and Wiley fingerprint a headless Chromium too.",
    "⭐_what_this_settles": "The reachable open-access EMC survival literature is EXACTLY the five papers already read. Three more are free for a human with a browser and unreachable by any automated route this program has; six are closed.",
    "⛔_and_the_line_that_is_not_crossed": "The next rung would be defeating bot protection, and this program does not build that. A paper a machine cannot fetch is recorded as unreachable; that IS the finding.",
